    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive outlook for August 21 is anchored by high-ceiling matchups against weak-to-middling arms. **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Kyle Tucker** (77.20) represent our elite tier for the day. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 16% park adjustment and a 14% platoon edge against Peralta, while the slow delivery of the opposing starter provides an additional boost to his stolen base potential. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** thrives in his matchup against Chandler, where the favorable SP skill rating (+19%) and a positive platoon adjustment solidify his role as a daily anchor. **Andy Pages** (72.74) is also a strong play, leveraging the same favorable SP matchup and the stolen base efficiency gained against Chandler\u2019s delivery tempo.\n\nOur bench decisions were dictated by a strict adherence to our 40.0 efficiency floor. **Dominic Smith** (37.94) came the closest to cracking the lineup, but the combination of Misiorowski\u2019s elite 2.09 xERA and a poor park adjustment pushed him just below the threshold. We are also monitoring the IL status of **Jordan Westburg** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, both of whom remain sidelined. While players like **Nasim Nunez** (51.84) and **Heliot Ramos** (50.95) are hovering near the marginal range, we are starting them to chase stolen base upside\u2014a critical priority given the scarcity of the category.\n\nRisks for today include the difficult matchup for **Drake Baldwin**, who faces Misiorowski\u2019s 2.09 xERA, forcing his score down to 45.76. Furthermore, **Luis Robert Jr.** (41.50) is starting despite a poor 15% platoon disadvantage, teetering dangerously close to our bench floor; he remains in the lineup purely to maintain our stolen base profile against a targetable Burke. We are operating with a clear directive: maximize daily efficiency scores while aggressively harvesting stolen bases against pitchers with slower-than-average deliveries, such as the trio of Gusto, Peralta, and Chandler.",
